You wear a vest (20 lb / 14 lb) the whole way. First come 50 strict pull-ups, then 100 hand-release push-ups, then a 5K run. There is no kipping on the pull-ups and your hands leave the floor on every push-up, so your upper body is spent long before the run starts. The 5K in a vest then tests how much you saved.',
   '[{"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}, {"name": "Hand-Release Push-Ups", "reps": "100", "tip": "Chest and thighs touch the floor, lift your hands, then press back up to a straight-arm plank.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "5 km", "tip": "Settle into a pace you can hold. Your arms will be tired, so relax your shoulders.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
