   '["Plan the 50 strict pull-ups as sets of 3 to 5 with short rests, because strict reps fade fast.", "Keep your body in a straight line on the hand-release push-ups and lift your hands just off the floor.", "Sets of 10 push-ups with a few breaths between them usually beat long sets followed by long rests.", "Strap the vest tight and high so it does not bounce on the run.", "Take the first kilometer of the run easy and let your breathing settle."]'::jsonb,
   'Drop the vest, or use a lighter one. Replace strict pull-ups with banded strict pull-ups or ring rows, and do the hand-release push-ups from your knees or on a raised surface. Cut the reps to 30 pull-ups and 60 push-ups and run 3 km if 5K is too long for now.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Severin workout?", "answer": "For time: 50 strict pull-ups, 100 hand-release push-ups and a 5K run, wearing a 20 lb / 14 lb vest."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Severin?", "answer": "150 reps: 50 strict pull-ups and 100 hand-release push-ups, plus a 5K run."}, {"question": "Do I wear the vest for the whole workout?", "answer": "Yes. CrossFit lists the vest as part of the Rx without limiting it to one part, so wear it for the pull-ups, push-ups and run."}, {"question": "Who was Severin?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Severin W. Summers III, 43, of Bentonia, Mississippi, of the 2nd Battalion, 20th Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Aug. 2, 2009, in Qole Gerdsar, Afghanistan, after his vehicle was struck by a command-wire improvised explosive device."}]'::jsonb,
