You do 7 rounds of 11 deadlifts at your own body weight, then a 100 m sprint. That is 77 deadlifts and 700 m of sprinting. The load is moderate for most people, but sprinting right after each set means your heart rate never comes down. Keeping your back flat on the late rounds is the real test.',
   '[{"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "11", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs, and stand all the way up. Load the bar to your body weight.", "rx_men": "Bodyweight", "rx_women": "Bodyweight"}, {"name": "Sprint", "reps": "100 m", "tip": "Run hard, but stay in control. Use the walk back to the bar to breathe."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Load the bar to your own body weight", "Keep your back flat on every rep", "Sprint fast but stay smooth"]'::jsonb,
   '["Weigh yourself before class and round the bar to the nearest plate you have.", "Set your back before every rep, even when you go unbroken.", "Touch and go only if your position stays the same; otherwise reset each rep.", "Sprint at a pace you can repeat 7 times, not an all-out first sprint.", "Shake out your grip on the way back to the bar."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the deadlift to 50 to 75 percent of your body weight. Replace the sprint with a fast 100 m run, or row 100 m if you cannot run. Newer athletes can do 5 rounds.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Sham workout?", "answer": "7 rounds for time of 11 bodyweight deadlifts and a 100 m sprint."}, {"question": "How heavy is the deadlift in Sham?", "answer": "Your own body weight, for men and women."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Sham?", "answer": "77 deadlifts, plus 700 m of sprinting."}, {"question": "Who was Sham?", "answer": "U.S. Air Force Staff Sgt. David \"Sham\" Wieger, 28, of North Huntingdon, Pennsylvania, a special agent with Detachment 303 at Travis Air Force Base, California. He died on Nov. 1, 2007, near Balad Air Base, Iraq, of wounds sustained when an improvised explosive device struck his vehicle."}]'::jsonb,
