You run 5 miles in 5-minute pieces. After each 5 minutes of running, you stop and do 50 squats and 50 push-ups, then start the next 5-minute run. You keep going until you have covered 5 miles. A faster runner finishes in fewer intervals, so fewer sets of squats and push-ups. CrossFit does not say whether you do a set after the last stretch of running.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "5 miles total, in 5-minute intervals", "tip": "Use a watch. Stop when 5 minutes are up and note how far you have gone."}, {"name": "Air Squats", "reps": "50 after each 5-minute run", "tip": "Hips below your knees, then stand all the way up."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "50 after each 5-minute run", "tip": "Chest to the floor and lock your arms at the top. Break them up early."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Run each 5-minute interval at a steady pace", "Break the push-ups early", "Track your distance as you go"]'::jsonb,
