   'Drop the vest, or use a lighter one. Replace the rope climb with a climb to a lower height or 3 lying-to-standing rope pulls. Walk part of the run if needed.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Sisson workout?", "answer": "As many rounds as possible in 20 minutes of 1 rope climb to 15 ft, 5 burpees and a 200 m run, wearing a 20 lb / 14 lb vest."}, {"question": "How is Sisson scored?", "answer": "Total rounds plus any extra reps. CrossFit does not say how to count a partial run, so if time runs out mid-run, note where you stopped."}, {"question": "What if I cannot climb a rope?", "answer": "Climb to a lower height, or do 3 lying-to-standing rope pulls for each climb."}, {"question": "Who was Sisson?", "answer": "U.S. Army 2nd Lt. Justin Sisson, 23, of the 1st Battalion, 506th Infantry Regiment, 4th Brigade Combat Team, 101st Airborne Division. He died on June 3, 2013, from wounds caused by a suicide bomber in Chamkani, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
