You run 6 km, then do 60 burpee pull-ups. CrossFit says that if you have body armor or a 30 lb vest, you should wear it. The run is long enough to tire your legs, and then each burpee pull-up asks you to drop to the floor, jump to the bar and pull. Going steady on both halves is the way through.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "6 km", "tip": "Run a pace you could hold for longer. You still have 60 hard reps to go.", "rx_men": "30 lb vest or body armor (if you have one)"}, {"name": "Burpee Pull-Ups", "reps": "60", "tip": "Chest to the floor, jump to the bar, and pull until your chin clears it.", "rx_men": "30 lb vest or body armor (if you have one)"}]'::jsonb,
