You complete 100 thrusters (135 lb / 95 lb), 100 chest-to-bar pull-ups and a 6 mile run. CrossFit lets you split the thrusters, pull-ups and run however you like, so you can mix them into rounds. That freedom helps, but the total work is huge. Plan your rounds before you start and expect to be out there well over an hour.',
   '[{"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "100", "tip": "Front squat below parallel, then drive the bar overhead in one motion.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "100", "tip": "Pull until your chest touches the bar. Use small sets to save your grip."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "6 miles", "tip": "Split the run into pieces between your sets and keep each one easy."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Plan your rounds before you start", "Keep thruster sets small and steady", "Eat and drink before a session this long"]'::jsonb,
