You do 8 rounds of a 600 m run, 11 weighted pull-ups, 11 walking lunges holding two kettlebells and 11 kettlebell thrusters. CrossFit gives one load, 53 lb / 35 lb, and does not say whether the thrusters use one kettlebell or two. The 4.8 km of running plus heavy lunges makes this a long leg grinder.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "600 m", "tip": "A steady pace you can hold for 8 rounds."}, {"name": "Weighted Pull-Ups", "reps": "11", "tip": "Hold the kettlebell between your feet or on a belt, and pull until your chin clears the bar.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Walking Lunges", "reps": "11", "tip": "Hold a kettlebell in each hand, back knee kisses the floor, stand tall each step.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Thrusters", "reps": "11", "tip": "Squat with the bells in the front rack, then drive them overhead in one motion.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
