   'Use lighter kettlebells, such as 35 lb / 26 lb, or do the pull-ups without weight. Replace weighted pull-ups with regular pull-ups or ring rows. Cut the run to 400 m or do 5 or 6 rounds.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Strange workout?", "answer": "8 rounds for time of a 600 m run, 11 weighted pull-ups, 11 walking lunges with two kettlebells and 11 kettlebell thrusters. The load is 53 lb / 35 lb."}, {"question": "Do the thrusters use one kettlebell or two?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Pick one option and note it with your time."}, {"question": "Are the 11 lunges counted per leg?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Count each step as one rep, or 11 per leg, and note which one you chose."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Strange?", "answer": "264 reps: 88 weighted pull-ups, 88 walking lunges and 88 kettlebell thrusters, plus 4,800 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Strange?", "answer": "U.S. Navy Cryptologist Technician (Collection) Petty Officer 1st Class (Expeditionary Warfare Specialist) Michael J. Strange, 25, of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. He died on Aug. 6, 2011, of wounds suffered when his unit''s helicopter crashed in Wardak Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
