   '["Ride the bike at a steady effort, because you still have 94 reps to do in each round.", "On the lunges, try the dumbbell in the goblet or the shoulder position and use the one you can hold longest.", "Break the toes-to-bars into sets of 5 to 7 from the first round.", "Keep your body in a straight line on the push-ups, and rest in a plank or on your knees, not with your hips sagging.", "On the snatches, pull the dumbbell close and punch it overhead, switching hands at the bottom."]'::jsonb,
