   'T.J. honors U.S. Marine Corps Pfc. Anthony "TJ" Antell Jr., 35, of Arlington, Texas, the owner of CrossFit Abattoir. He died on May 2, 2016, from a gunshot wound when he tried to disarm a gunman at a local Walgreens.

Each round is 10 bench presses (185 lb / 125 lb), 10 strict pull-ups and one max set of thrusters (135 lb / 95 lb). You repeat the round until you reach 100 thrusters in total. The bigger your thruster sets, the fewer rounds of bench press and strict pull-ups you need. That makes every thruster set a choice between pushing on and saving your upper body.',
   '[{"name": "Bench Press", "reps": "10", "tip": "Lower the bar to your chest under control and press to lockout. Use a spotter or safeties.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar."}, {"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "Max set (100 total)", "tip": "One unbroken set each round. Squat below parallel and drive the bar overhead.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Go long on the early thruster sets", "Bench with a spotter or safeties", "Break the strict pull-ups if you need to"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set up the bench and a squat rack side by side so you can move between them quickly.", "Use safety arms or a spotter on the bench press, because your chest and arms will be very tired.", "Each thruster set ends when you put the bar down, so stay in a good rhythm and breathe at the top.", "Break the strict pull-ups into small sets early, such as 4, 3 and 3.", "Keep a running count of your thrusters on a whiteboard."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the bench press to 135 lb / 85 lb and the thrusters to 95 lb / 65 lb, or less. Replace strict pull-ups with banded pull-ups or ring rows. Cut the target to 50 thrusters.',
