   'T.U.P. honors U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Michael H. Simpson, 30, of San Antonio, Texas, who was nicknamed "The Unquiet Professional." He was assigned to the 4th Battalion, 1st Special Forces Group (Airborne), and died on May 1, 2013, from injuries caused by an improvised explosive device on April 27, 2013, in Arian, Afghanistan.

You do 15-12-9-6-3 reps of power cleans, pull-ups, front squats and pull-ups again, with the barbell at 135 lb / 95 lb. That is 45 power cleans, 45 front squats and 90 pull-ups. The two sets of pull-ups in each round tax your grip right before and after the cleans, so pull-up pacing decides your time.',
   '[{"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "15-12-9-6-3", "tip": "Catch the bar above parallel with your elbows up.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "15-12-9-6-3", "tip": "Pull until your chin clears the bar."}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "15-12-9-6-3", "tip": "Elbows up and squat below parallel. Clean the bar to your shoulders to start.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "15-12-9-6-3", "tip": "The second set of the round. Break it early if your grip is fading."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Break the first round of pull-ups early", "Keep the bar close on the cleans", "The rounds shrink fast, so keep moving"]'::jsonb,
