   'time',
   'Tama honors Cpl. Luke Tamatea, 31, of Kawerau, New Zealand, who served with the 1st Battalion Royal New Zealand Infantry Regiment. He was killed by a roadside bomb on Aug. 19, 2012, in the Bamyan Province of Afghanistan, during his second tour there. He was an avid CrossFit athlete who practiced long farmers carries to prepare for Special Forces selection.

You carry a barbell in one hand for 800 m, 400 m and 200 m, getting heavier each time (45, 95, 135 lb / 35, 65, 95 lb). Between the carries you do 31 toes-to-bars and 31 push-ups, then 31 front squats after the first carry and 31 hang power cleans after the second. Holding a long barbell by its middle in one hand makes your grip and trunk work the whole way.',
   '[{"name": "Barbell Farmers Carry", "reps": "800 m, single-arm", "tip": "Hold the barbell by its middle in one hand so it stays level. Walk tall.", "rx_men": "45 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Toes-to-Bar", "reps": "31", "tip": "Hang from the bar and swing your toes up to touch it between your hands."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "31", "tip": "Chest to the floor and lock your arms at the top."}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "31", "tip": "Elbows up and squat below parallel.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Barbell Farmers Carry", "reps": "400 m, single-arm", "tip": "Heavier bar. Brace your trunk so you do not lean away from it.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Toes-to-Bar", "reps": "31", "tip": "Your grip is tired from the carry, so break them up early."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "31", "tip": "Short sets with quick rests."}, {"name": "Hang Power Cleans", "reps": "31", "tip": "Start above the knee, then pull and catch above parallel.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Barbell Farmers Carry", "reps": "200 m, single-arm", "tip": "The heaviest bar. Set it down and reset when you need to.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Hold the bar exactly at its middle", "Break the toes-to-bars before your grip fails", "Expect to set the heavy bar down on the last carry"]'::jsonb,
   '["Mark the middle of the bar with chalk so you can find the balance point fast.", "Squeeze hard and keep your shoulder pulled down so the bar does not tip.", "CrossFit does not say whether you may switch hands during a carry. Decide before you start and note it with your time.", "Break the toes-to-bars into sets of 5 to 8, because your grip is already working on the carries.", "Load your front squat and hang power clean bars before you start, so you only walk from station to station."]'::jsonb,
   'Use lighter bars, an empty training bar or a dumbbell or kettlebell for the carries, and shorten them to 400, 200 and 100 m. Swap toes-to-bars for hanging knee raises, do push-ups on a raised surface, and lower the front squats and cleans to 65 lb / 45 lb. Cut the reps to 21 if needed.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Tama workout?", "answer": "For time: an 800 m single-arm barbell farmers carry, 31 toes-to-bars, 31 push-ups, 31 front squats, a 400 m single-arm carry, 31 toes-to-bars, 31 push-ups, 31 hang power cleans and a 200 m single-arm carry."}, {"question": "What are the weights in Tama?", "answer": "Men: carries at 45, 95 and 135 lb, front squats at 95 lb and hang power cleans at 135 lb. Women: carries at 35, 65 and 95 lb, front squats at 65 lb and hang power cleans at 95 lb."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Tama?", "answer": "186 reps: 62 toes-to-bars, 62 push-ups, 31 front squats and 31 hang power cleans, plus 1,400 m of carrying."}, {"question": "Can I switch hands on the carry?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Pick one approach and note it with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Tama?", "answer": "Cpl. Luke Tamatea, 31, of Kawerau, New Zealand, of the 1st Battalion Royal New Zealand Infantry Regiment. He was killed by a roadside bomb on Aug. 19, 2012, while serving with the New Zealand Defence Force in the Bamyan Province of Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
