   'Taylor honors U.S. Army Spc. David Wayne Taylor, 20, of Dixon, Kentucky, who was assigned to the 2nd Battalion, 508th Parachute Infantry Regiment, 4th Brigade Combat Team, 82nd Airborne Division at Fort Bragg, North Carolina. He died on March 29, 2012, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan, from wounds sustained in an accident at an ammunition supply point.

You wear a vest (20 lb / 14 lb) for 4 rounds of a 400 m run and 5 burpee muscle-ups. That is only 20 muscle-ups, but each one starts with a burpee and the vest adds weight to every pull. CrossFit does not say whether to use rings or a bar. The runs are short enough to push, so the muscle-ups decide your time.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Run hard but controlled. Your heart rate needs to settle before the muscle-ups.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}, {"name": "Burpee Muscle-Ups", "reps": "5", "tip": "Chest to the floor, jump to the rings or bar, then do one muscle-up.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "14 lb vest"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Take the muscle-ups as quick singles", "Breathe before each jump to the rings", "Strap the vest tight"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set the rings or bar at a height you can reach with a small jump from the burpee.", "Do each burpee muscle-up as a single and take a breath before every jump.", "Use the last 50 m of each run to slow down a little and bring your breathing down.", "Keep the vest snug and high so it does not shift during the kip.", "Use the same rings or bar for every round, and note which one you chose with your time."]'::jsonb,
   'Drop the vest, or use a lighter one. Replace each burpee muscle-up with a burpee plus 2 pull-ups and 2 dips, or a burpee plus 3 ring rows. Walk part of the runs if needed.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Taylor workout?", "answer": "4 rounds for time of a 400 m run and 5 burpee muscle-ups, wearing a 20 lb / 14 lb vest."}, {"question": "Ring or bar muscle-ups?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Use the one you have and note it with your time."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Taylor?", "answer": "20 burpee muscle-ups, plus 1,600 m of running."}, {"question": "Who was Taylor?", "answer": "U.S. Army Spc. David Wayne Taylor, 20, of Dixon, Kentucky, of the 2nd Battalion, 508th Parachute Infantry Regiment, 82nd Airborne Division. He died on March 29, 2012, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan, from wounds sustained in an accident at an ammunition supply point."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GMalBAB3mtI');
